## Step 5: Extract specific forensic metadata

To display important metadata fields, execute:

```
exiftool -FileName -FileSize -FileType -MIMEType -ImageWidth -ImageHeight -FileCreateDate -FileModifyDate -DateTimeOriginal -Make -Model "C:\Users\mkavi\OneDrive\Pictures\goku-cosmic-evolution-nw-1366x768.jpg"
```

To view metadata grouped by category, execute:

```
exiftool -a -G1 -s "C:\Users\mkavi\OneDrive\Pictures\goku-cosmic-evolution-nw-1366x768.jpg"
```

## Step 6: Save the metadata as forensic evidence

Execute this command:

```
exiftool "C:\Users\mkavi\OneDrive\Pictures\goku-cosmic-evolution-nw-1366x768.jpg" > "C:\DMF\image_metadata.txt"
```

This creates:

```
C:\DMF\image_metadata.txt
```

Open the text file to review the extracted metadata.

